<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Massasoit</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1581–1661</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ousamequin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Massasoit, also called Ousamequin, was the sachem, or paramount leader, of the Wampanoag in the early 17th century, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sowams">Sowams</a> in present-day Rhode Island. In March 1621 he made a treaty of mutual defence with the Pilgrims of Plymouth Colony, and that autumn he shared the harvest feast later remembered as the first Thanksgiving. He kept the peace with the English until his death around 1661.</p></div>
